course: dictionary
lesson: 5743
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A loudspeaker is a device that makes sound louder, so that many people can hear one voice or one piece of music. The sentence around the word tells you what it means. «A loudspeaker uses electricity in a coil next to a magnet to push a cone in and out, making sound waves in the air.» Here it is a thing you can point to.
explain: Some words have a second meaning. Someone might say, «Put the call on loudspeaker» (on a phone). That means everyone in the room can hear, not just the person holding the phone. Always check: swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Clues can come from the situation too. A station announcement comes over the loudspeaker, so you know it is a machine that sends a voice to a crowd. Ask yourself: is this word a thing, or a way of making sound reach many people?
fact: A loudspeaker turns electrical signals into sound.
fact: Inside, a magnet and a coil make a cone move in and out, pushing air to make sound waves.
fact: «Speaker» is a shorter word that people often use for loudspeaker.
fact: «On loudspeaker» means so everyone in the room can hear.
fact: In one experiment, «beavers piled sticks on a loudspeaker playing the sound of running water», which shows that much of their building is instinct, not planning.
exercise: «A loudspeaker uses electricity in a coil next to a magnet to push a cone in and out.» In this sentence, what is a loudspeaker? | A room where music is played | A person who gives a talk | A large, loud animal | *A device that turns electrical signals into sound
exercise: Someone says, «Put the call on loudspeaker.» What does it mean? | So nobody can hear the call | *So everyone in the room can hear | So the phone is switched off | So the call is private
exercise: Which word is a shorter way of saying loudspeaker? | *speaker | cone | magnet | coil
test: Where might you hear an announcement «over the loudspeaker»? | Inside a book | In a bath | Under the sea | *At a station, in a school or during a fire drill
test: In the beaver experiment, what did the loudspeaker play? | Complete silence | The sound of a train | The sound of birds singing | *The sound of running water
exam: Which sentence about a loudspeaker is true? | It is always made of wood | *It makes voices louder so many people can hear | It only works in the dark | It is a kind of fish
